    "subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is the source clip for the target edit: a 5.17-second, 24 fps, single continuous static medium close-up at eye level of a man framed from the chest up, standing in a blurred cool blue-grey brick alley with one large bright white patch of sky in the upper right and two blurred pale-yellow lamp shapes low in the frame; at the first frame he stands at the left of the frame holding a lit cigarette beside his mouth, a small wisp of smoke leaving his lips as he pulls it away, throws the cigarette down to the ground inside the first second, then sways and rolls his head in place, blows out one thick cloud of smoke that covers his face, and spreads his arms out to the sides.\n<Picture 1> is a character sheet of the replacement character: a close-up of his face, a full-body front view and a back view of the same man.\n<Subject 1> is that man, exactly as drawn in <Picture 1>: a tall ornate gold crown pierced crosswise by a long gold pin, a black topknot, long straight black hair falling past his shoulders, thick level black brows, a thin black moustache, a long pointed black goatee, bare unpainted skin, a calm face with his lips closed, and a pale ice-blue ankle-length robe with wide sleeves, a white crossed inner collar, a dark blue embroidered placket down the centre of the chest and matching dark blue embroidered cuffs, worn over white trousers and black cloth shoes.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing + reference generation] The target video is an edited version of <Video 1>. The man in <Video 1> is replaced by <Subject 1> from <Picture 1>, who keeps the same place in frame, the same head size, the same timing, the same dance and the same one thick exhale of smoke; his whole outfit is the pale ice-blue robe of <Picture 1>, worn from his throat to his ankles. The cigarette, the small wisp of smoke at the start, the thick cloud of smoke that rolls across his face, the brick alley, the bright patch of sky, the two pale-yellow lamp shapes and the static camera of <Video 1> are kept unchanged. His face stays bare and quiet, with his lips closed and his expression grave apart from the one exhale.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Video 1> (shot structure and camera): fully_preserved - one continuous static medium close-up at eye level with a fixed lens, no cut, no zoom and no camera move, the man standing at the left of the frame at the start and drifting toward the centre as he sways, the brick wall out of focus behind him.\n<Video 1> (person): partially_preserved - the head position, head size, shoulder line, stance, weight shift, body sway and arm gestures are kept, while his face, headwear, hair and clothing are replaced by <Subject 1>.\n<Video 1> (performance): partially_preserved - the lit cigarette raised beside his mouth at the first frame, the small wisp of smoke that leaves his lips as the cigarette is pulled away, the small downward flick of the wrist that throws it to the ground within the first second, the single thick exhale just under two seconds in that covers his face, the slow sway in place, the rolling tilts of the head, the loose fist drawn across his chest and the final spread of both arms out to the sides keep their original order, rhythm and amplitude; apart from that one exhale his face stays calm and closed-mouthed, his eyes lowered or half-closed and his lips resting in a flat quiet line.\n<Picture 1>: attribute_transfer - the gold crown and its crosswise pin, the topknot, the long straight black hair, the thick level brows, the thin moustache, the long pointed goatee, the bare clean skin, the white crossed inner collar, the dark blue embroidered placket and cuffs, and the pale ice-blue ankle-length wide-sleeved robe are transferred onto the dancing man, with natural body proportions matching the man in <Video 1>.\n<Video 1> (smoke): fully_preserved - the small wisp at his lips in the first frame, then one thick pale grey cloud that leaves his mouth about 1.8 seconds in, rolls up over his mouth, nose and eyes and hides most of his face around two seconds, before thinning and drifting up past his left temple and out of frame.\n<Video 1> (ending): fully_preserved - in the last second he holds a loose sway with his head tipped back to his left, his eyes closed, his lips closed and both arms spread out low at his sides, and he keeps that pose until the final frame.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] Realistic live-action street footage, soft cool daylight with a warm rim along his right side, fine film grain and a shallow depth of field. The camera holds a static medium close-up at eye level on one man, <Subject 1>, framed from the chest up, his head close to the top edge of the frame with the crown near the top border. Behind him a cool blue-grey brick alley runs out of focus, with one large bright white patch of sky in the upper right and two blurred pale-yellow lamp shapes low in the frame. At the first frame he stands at the left of the frame with his right hand raised beside his mouth, a lit cigarette held between his first two fingers, a small wisp of pale smoke trailing from the cigarette and out of his lips as he draws it away, his head tipped down and turned to his left, his eyes lowered and his lips closed. Within the first second he flicks the cigarette away with a small downward toss of his wrist so it drops out of frame onto the ground, and his hand falls back to his side. About 1.8 seconds in, with his head thrown back and his eyes closed, he blows out one thick cloud of pale grey smoke: his lips part into a small round blowing shape with the corners of his mouth level, and the cloud rolls up over his mouth, over his nose and across his eyes, hiding most of his face at its densest around two seconds, then it thins and drifts up past his left temple and out of frame. For the rest of the clip he sways in place, his weight shifting from foot to foot: his head rolls back and to his left, his chin lifts, his eyes stay closed or half-closed, his right hand draws across his chest in a loose fist, and near the end both arms spread out to the sides at waist height in a loose shrug while his head tips back and his shoulders roll. Between the exhale and the final frame his lips stay closed and relaxed in a flat quiet line, his brows stay level, and his face keeps the calm, grave, bare-skinned expression of <Picture 1>. The pale ice-blue robe covers him from his throat to his ankles: the white crossed inner collar sits at his neck, the dark blue embroidered placket runs down the centre of his chest, the wide ice-blue sleeves with dark blue embroidered cuffs swing with every arm sweep, and the long skirt of the robe moves with his sway. The long straight black hair, the thin moustache and the long pointed goatee shift with each head turn, and the gold crown with its long crosswise pin stays fixed on his head and catches the pale light. His head size, head position, shoulder line and movement path follow the man in <Video 1> exactly, and only the person himself is different: the face, the brows, the moustache, the goatee, the crown, the topknot, the hair and the pale ice-blue robe come from <Picture 1>, with clean bare skin keeping a natural skin texture and natural lip colour. The brick wall, the bright sky patch and the two lamp shapes stay exactly as in <Video 1>. Only this one man is in the frame.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA low city hum beyond the brick alley, his slow breathing as he sways, the soft puff of the single exhale, cloth rustling with each arm sweep, cloth shoes scuffing on the ground, and the small dry tap of the cigarette as it lands on the ground.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
